  "10": {
    "action": "confirm",
    "canonical": "Do not build repeated or nested sequences with the * operator when the elements are mutable, because s*n duplicates references to the SAME object so all copies share it; build independent copies with a comprehension such as [[] for _ in range(n)] or [list(a) for _ in range(n)]."
  },
  "11": {
    "action": "confirm",
    "canonical": "Understand that augmented assignment (+=, *=) mutates a mutable target in place (via __iadd__/__imul__) so every other reference observes the change, but rebinds an immutable target to a new object; this explains why += on a list inside a tuple both mutates and raises, so avoid putting mutable items in tuples."
  },
